From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:18:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: Skip GPU initialization for a KMS-only device

msm_open() is shared by drivers registering display and rendering
nodes. The KMS-only driver intentionally has no GPU platform device.
Calling load_gpu() when opening that node produces an error on every
open.

Initialize the GPU on devices advertising DRIVER_RENDER. Keep file
context initialization for all nodes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
index f3d2eaa04..8c6098d49 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
@@ -268,7 +268,8 @@ static int msm_open(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_file *file)
 	/* For now, load gpu on open.. to avoid the requirement of having
 	 * firmware in the initrd.
 	 */
-	load_gpu(dev);
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER))
+		load_gpu(dev);
 
 	return context_init(dev, file);
 }
